{
  "_comment": "Frozen patient-level train/validation/test splits for the PortPy benchmark tasks, approximately 80/10/10 of every patient in the dataset. Splits are at the patient level: all beamlets and all dose voxels of a patient belong to the same partition, which prevents train/test leakage in Task 1, where one patient contributes thousands of beamlets. Task 2 is site specific and uses the lung or prostate entry directly. Task 1 pools the two sites, i.e. it uses the union of the corresponding partitions, because beamlet dose is governed by radiation physics and anatomy rather than by disease site. Task 3 is an optimization task and has no training partition; its instances are specified per patient. Load with DataExplorer.load_config_data_splits().",
